# Privacy Policy for Legend Run

**Last updated: 2 October 2026**

Legend Run ("the app", "we", "us") is developed and published by Steven. This
policy explains what data the app processes, why, and who it is shared with.

## Summary

Legend Run has no accounts of its own and no server of its own. Your game
progress is stored on your device. If you are signed in to Game Center (iOS)
or Google Play Games (Android), your scores and achievements are shared with
that service so they can appear on its global leaderboards. The app also
shows third-party advertising, collects anonymous usage analytics and sends
crash reports, and those services process some data about your device. The
details are below.

## Data stored on your device

The following is saved locally on your device using the operating system's
standard app storage:

- Your best scores (normal and Blind mode) and your lifetime points
- Which worlds you have unlocked and which one you selected
- Sound, vibration, Blind mode and performance preferences
- Whether you have seen the how-to-play hints

This data is not sent to us. Deleting the app removes it permanently.

## Online leaderboards and achievements

The app uses **Apple Game Center** on iOS and **Google Play Games** on Android
for global leaderboards and achievements. If you are signed in to one of these
services:

- Your scores and unlocked achievements are sent to Apple or Google and shown
  with your Game Center / Play Games player name and profile on their
  leaderboards.
- The app reads your player name and your leaderboard rank to show them in the
  game.

We never see or store your Apple or Google account details. Signing in is
optional; if you are not signed in, nothing is sent and the game works
normally. These services are governed by their own policies:

- Apple Privacy Policy: https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/
- Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

You can sign out, hide your profile or reset your Game Center / Play Games
data at any time in your device's Game Center settings or in the Google Play
Games app.

## Advertising

The app displays advertisements supplied by **Google AdMob**. To serve ads,
Google may collect and process:

- Your device's advertising identifier (IDFA on iOS, Advertising ID on Android)
- Device and connection information, such as device model, operating system
  version, language, and coarse location derived from IP address
- Information about your interaction with advertisements

**Consent in the EEA, the UK, Switzerland and some US states.** Where the law
requires it, the app shows a consent message from Google's User Messaging
Platform the first time you open it, and only requests ads as your choices
allow. You can review or change your choices at any time in the app under
**Settings → Privacy settings**.

**App Tracking Transparency (iOS).** Before any advertising identifier is used
for tracking, the app presents Apple's App Tracking Transparency prompt and
asks for your permission.

- If you **allow** tracking, Google may use your advertising identifier to show
  you personalised advertisements.
- If you **decline**, the app requests non-personalised advertisements. You will
  still see ads, but they will not be based on your advertising identifier.

You can change this choice at any time in **Settings → Privacy & Security →
Tracking** on iOS.

Google's handling of this data is governed by their own policies:

- Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy
- How Google uses information from partner sites and apps:
  https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites

## Analytics and crash reports

The app uses **Google Firebase Analytics** to understand how the game is used
in aggregate — for example how many players start a run, which worlds are
chosen, and where players stop playing. This data is collected in a form that
does not identify you personally, and includes anonymous event names, an
app-instance identifier, device model, operating system version, and country.

The app uses **Google Firebase Crashlytics** to receive a report when the app
crashes, so we can fix the problem. A crash report contains technical
information about the crash (such as the state of the app and the code that
failed), the device model, operating system version and an app-instance
identifier. It does not contain your name or contact details.

We use this data only to improve the game. Firebase is provided by Google and
is subject to the Google Privacy Policy linked above.

## Data we do not collect

We do not collect your name, email address, phone number, contacts, photos,
precise location, or any other personal information. The app has no sign-up
of its own, no messaging and no user-generated content.

## Children's privacy

Legend Run is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect
personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has
provided personal information through the app, contact us at the address below
and we will address it.

## Sharing your information

We do not sell your data. We do not share your data with anyone other than the
service providers named above (Apple Game Center, Google Play Games, Google
AdMob and Google Firebase), who process it on the terms of their own privacy
policies.

## Your rights and choices

- **Ad consent (EEA, UK, Switzerland, some US states):** in the app, Settings →
  Privacy settings.
- **Advertising tracking:** iOS — Settings → Privacy & Security → Tracking.
  Android — Settings → Google → Ads.
- **Leaderboards and achievements:** sign out of, or manage, Game Center
  (iOS Settings → Game Center) or Google Play Games.
- **Local data:** delete the app to remove all data stored on your device.

